Implemented:
- host/forge_bridge.py (development only): records CHOMPI through an audio
  interface (sounddevice/WASAPI), plays bounded test tones (<= -6 dBFS,
  plans use -18) into line in, measures level/pitch/clicks/onset/noise and
  draws spectrogram PNGs; drives the virtual panel and probe of the
  development firmware; runs JSON plans into report folders
  (report.json, summary.md, WAV + PNG per capture). Human-judgement steps
  are asked, or marked needs-human with --unattended.
- forge_host.py: panel/probe messages and replies (0x46/0x47).
- tests/hardware/smoke.json: automatable parts of TEST_SESSION.
- host/bridge-requirements.txt (numpy, sounddevice).

Software-tested: tests/test_bridge.py (analysis on synthetic signals,
WAV/PNG files, gestures, plans against the simulated CHOMPI with fake
audio); make test 65 Python tests pass. smoke.json runs end to end on the
simulator with no step errors (its audio checks fail there by design).

Hardware-verified: nothing. Real audio devices and the dev firmware's
panel/probe on CHOMPI are untested.

